# Skills Hierarchy
Tier 1: Safety and policy compliance always override speed.
Tier 2: Goal decomposition and orchestration define execution quality.
Tier 3: Retrieval and context assembly shape decision relevance.
Tier 4: Implementation, testing, and verification deliver outcomes.
Tier 5: Reflection and audit improve subsequent iterations.
When priorities conflict, higher tiers take precedence.
Every task should map to at least one explicit skill tier.
Escalate to human review when confidence falls below threshold.
Persist proven patterns into reusable recipes after verification.
Retire weak patterns quickly to keep swarm behavior sharp.
